    "turn_text": "Dakota. She had family in the area. He had been a police officer in Alameda County, got injured, wanted to go back into police work and found this job in Iowa. And he brought the 911 system there. They didn't have 911. He started the Boys and Girls Club and the Mothers Against Drunk Driving Chapter. And the DUI arrests in the town went from like four the year that he was not there to 40 this first year there. And as he says, it wasn't because they developed a drinking problem. Like they started enforcing the law. And a lot of people in this small town, a good old boys network as he would call it, they just didn't like that. And so it came to a head and this is very typical, this is very small town Iowa fashion at the county fair. My dad gets a phone call from the fire chief, and the fire chief says, sir, we have parked in the fire lane, the mayor and a city council member, and they won't move their cars. They said they can park wherever they want. I knew how this story is going to end as soon as my dad started to tell me once I was older, because I've lived under his strict rules. He told the fire chief, if they don't move,",
