    "turn_idx": 200,
    "turn_text": "Most of them went to college at a time when college was affordable. Since 1980, however, the cost of college has gone up 306% with inflation adjusted. And if their kids went to college, if they're millionaires before they went to Congress, their kids didn't take on student loan debt. So it was just a disconnect. So Speaker Pelosi asked me in 2014 to take the younger members and create a group to go across the country, learn the issues, and be a voice for that generation. We called it Future Forum. I led that for the last five years. This election, we crossed 50, over 50 members in our 40s and under. I see an opportunity as president to work with the next generation Congress that can take on these issues of climate chaos, of student loan debt, of being safe in our community. And we have a Congress now that looks more like America. It's not there yet. And that's why I think you have to get rid of the dirty money and the dirty maps. But we have an opportunity to really make a difference on these issues. Do you feel like being out front about your own personal life? You talk about being a renter. You talk about your student loan debt. There was an article on a local paper recently about some of your financial challenges. And we've seen this also with Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez talking about how she couldn't afford to move to DC before she got sworn in, things like that. Do you find that people like, like that on the campaign trail or do you ever get pushed back? Like, why should we trust you if you, you know? I think about that a lot. I want to be honest",
